    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1050">

                <pb facs="1311" n="1297" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.20 Missions/11–1545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Beaulac</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-16T20:00:00-05:00">November 16,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>346. Uriel 557, Nov. 15, 10 a.m. Note 922 not reed. Assuming it deals with same
                    subject as 901, Dept authorizes return of both notes in your discretion but
                    recommends matter be handled informally and orally with Foreign Minister.<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d1050-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1050-f1" n="37" xml:id="d1050-f1-content">
                <p>The Ambassador indicated in his telegram 564, November 17, 1945, 11 a.m., that
                    the notes were returned (834.20 Missions/11–1745).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
